  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/82869B">Definition <span data-tag="82869B">7.2.1.1</span>.</a>dimension!homotopyhomotopy dimension homotopy dimension!finite Let $\calX $ be an $\infty $-topos. We shall say that $\calX $ has <em>homotopy dimension $\leq n$</em> if every $n$-connective object $U \in \calX $ admits a global section $1_{\calX } \rightarrow U$. We say that $\calX $ has <em>finite homotopy dimension</em> if there exists $n \geq 0$ such that $\calX $ has homotopy dimension $\leq n$. </p>
